A restaurant-style baked pasta combining garlic alfredo sauce, crumbled Italian sausage, marinara, and five melted Italian cheeses beneath a toasted Parmesan-panko crumb topping.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a25241416/five-cheese-ziti-al-forno-olive-garden-copycat/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 lb. sweet Italian sausage
- 1 lb. ziti pasta
- 4 tablespoons butter
- 2 cloves garlic, minced
- 4 tablespoons all-purpose flour
- 2 cups half-and-half
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- Pinch of red pepper flakes (optional)
- 1 cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese, divided
- 3 cups marinara sauce
- 2 cups shredded mozzarella cheese, divided
- ½ cup shredded fontina cheese
- ½ cup grated romano cheese
- ½ cup ricotta cheese
- ½ cup panko breadcrumbs
- Freshly chopped parsley, for garnish

## Instructions

1. **Cook and Drain the Sausage:** Place a skillet over medium heat and brown the bulk Italian sausage, breaking the meat into bite-sized crumbles with a spatula. Once browned with no remaining pink (roughly 6 to 8 minutes), pour off and discard rendered grease, then set the cooked meat aside.
2. **Boil Ziti and Prep Pan:** Set your oven to 375°F (190°C) and coat a 9x13-inch baking pan with nonstick spray. Cook the ziti in a large pot of salted boiling water until al dente—stopping 1 to 2 minutes earlier than box directions to ensure the pasta stays firm during baking. Drain well.
3. **Whisk Garlic Alfredo:** Melt the butter in a high-sided saucepan over medium heat. Stir in the minced garlic for 30 seconds until aromatic, then whisk in the flour and allow it to bubble for 1 minute into a blond roux. Slowly drizzle in the half-and-half while whisking vigorously to guarantee a silky texture. Simmer gently for 2 to 3 minutes until thickened, then fold in ½ cup of Parmesan, salt, black pepper, and chili flakes.
4. **Mix Pasta and Five Cheeses:** Take the pan off heat. Stir in the marinara sauce, drained sausage, ricotta, fontina, romano, and 1 cup of the mozzarella until the cheeses melt smoothly into the sauce. Add the drained ziti and fold gently until every tube is evenly coated.
5. **Layer and Top with Panko Crust:** Transfer the pasta mixture into the prepared baking dish. Spread the final cup of mozzarella across the top. In a small dish, mix the panko with the reserved ½ cup of Parmesan and sprinkle the mixture evenly over the cheese.
6. **Bake and Rest:** Bake uncovered for 25 to 30 minutes until the edges bubble vigorously and the breadcrumb topping turns golden and crisp. Allow the casserole to rest for 5 minutes before portioning; finish with fresh chopped parsley.

## Notes

- **Make-ahead:** You can assemble the entire dish ahead of time, cover tightly with foil, and refrigerate for up to 24 hours. When ready to bake, add 10–15 minutes to the covered baking time before uncovering to brown the topping.
- **Cheese substitutions:** Provolone or Asiago make great substitutes if Fontina or Romano are hard to find.
